        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Plants: Muehlenbeckia, Euptelea\n- Places: Southern Hemisphere, South America, Papua New Guinea, Australia, New Zealand, temperate locales north of the equator\n- Concepts: native range, introduction, genus, species, monogeneric family, flowering plants\n\nFacts:\n- Muehlenbeckia, also called the maidenhair genus, is native to the Southern Hemisphere, especially South America, Papua New Guinea, Australia, and New Zealand.\n- Muehlenbeckia has been introduced to temperate locales north of the equator by birds and by cultivation.\n- Euptelea is a genus of two species of flowering plants.\n- Euptelea belongs to the monogeneric family Eupteleaceae.",
